    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnĕus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		linum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of flax</i> or <i>lint, flaxen, linen-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vincula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 5, 510</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terga,</span>”
				<i>the linen lining of a shield</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10, 784</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 6, 13, § 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lanugo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					32, 10, 44, § 126</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pannis lineis involvere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					8, 10, 1</span></i>
			.—Also <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnĕum</span></b> , <i>a linen garment</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ezech.
				9, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10, 2</span></i>
		al.</div>
